,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Champion Homes, Inc. produces and sells factory-built housing in the United States and Canada. The company offers manufactured and modular homes, park models recreational vehicles and cabins, accessory dwelling units, commercial structures, and modular buildings for the single and multi-family markets. It builds homes under the Champion Homes, Genesis Homes, Skyline Homes, Regional Homes, Athens Park, Dutch Housing, Atlantic Homes, Excel Homes, Homes of Merit, New Era, J. Redman Homes, ScotBilt Homes, Shore Park, Silvercrest, and Titan Homes in the United States; and Moduline and SRI Homes brand names in western Canada. The company also provides construction service to install and set-up factory-built homes under the Champion Construction brand; operates a factory-direct manufactured home retail business under the Regional Homes, Titan Factory Direct, and Champion Homes Center brand names; and offers transportation services to manufactured housing and other industries. The company was formerly known as Skyline Champion Corporation and changed its name to Champion Homes, Inc. in August 2024. The company was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in Troy, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy Mark Larson | Chief Growth Officer, President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $290K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Champion Homes, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $5.0B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +29% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $270M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 33\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 49% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.49087164123209437},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sky Metals and Advance Metals Propose Spin-Out of Gold Assets","source":"smallcaps.com.au","link":"https://smallcaps.com.au/article/sky-metals-and-advance-metals-propose-spin-out-of-gold-assets","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794550303.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Advance Metals (ASX: AVM) and Sky Metals (ASX: SKY) Unveil Gold Spin-Out with ASX Listing Plans","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/ca/news/featured-news/advance-metals-asx-avm-and-sky-metals-asx-sky-unveil-gold-spin-out-with-asx-listing-plans","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794536820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Champion Homes (SKY) Dropped, What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-sky/champion-homes/news/champion-homes-sky-dropped-what-is-driving-attention-now","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794392933.418,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.931,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Champion Homes (SKY) Said on Its Q2 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/champion-homes-sky-said-q2-131419497.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794143659.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Third Avenue Management's Top Q3 2026 Move: D.R. Horton Inc